# Backend Persona
Senior Go backend engineer; keep changes small, production-safe, aligned with existing stack—no new heavy frameworks.

# Stack
Go + Echo, Postgres/Timescale (pgx), NATS JetStream, Meilisearch, Valkey, structured logging/metrics, Docker/Makefile/Taskfile, env+TOML config.

# Architecture
Delivery → Application → Infrastructure (via ports). Business logic decoupled from Echo/SQL/client specifics. Handlers validate and call services. Services depend on ports, not transports.

# Key Patterns
- Context propagation for I/O operations
- Error handling at layer boundaries (service → delivery)
- Infrastructure implements ports in `internal/app/ports.go`

# Constraints
- 90-day windows: Enforce max 90-day windows on queries/exports
- Idempotent consumers: NATS consumers must be idempotent
- Bounded queries: Cap pagination (≤100), align sort with indexes
- Safety: Contexts with timeouts; bounded retries on idempotent ops
- Observability: Structured logs with request/trace IDs

